WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.147
Open any drawer in your plant.

00:00:04.427 --> 00:00:08.873
If you cannot spot what is missing in two seconds, you do not have tool control.

00:00:09.473 --> 00:00:13.971
Mixed drawers lead to lost tools, duplicate purchases and wasted time.

00:00:14.251 --> 00:00:17.396
Small parts get mixed, and the wrong part gets used.

00:00:17.996 --> 00:00:23.076
Drawer partitions divide each drawer into fixed compartments, sized to the drawer height.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:27.251
Foam cut-outs go further, giving every tool its own shaped space.

00:00:27.531 --> 00:00:30.704
This is the 5S idea of 'a place for everything':

00:00:30.704 --> 00:00:34.406
an empty spot shows instantly that something is missing.

00:00:34.686 --> 00:00:38.864
Keep the heaviest tools in the lowest drawers, so the cabinet stays stable.

00:00:39.464 --> 00:00:42.556
One automotive electronics maker stores sensors,

00:00:42.556 --> 00:00:47.709
circuit boards and connectors in a nine-drawer Furnisys cabinet with partitions,

00:00:47.709 --> 00:00:49.899
plus spare compartments for later.

00:00:50.179 --> 00:00:53.762
A service centre uses foam cut-outs in mobile cabinets.

00:00:54.362 --> 00:00:57.170
Organise one drawer today and see the difference.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:00:59.454
Which drawer in your plant needs it most?

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:03.810
Comment below, and next, discover how flow racks deliver FIFO.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:08.655
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

